WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.333 --> 00:00:02.670
- I'm at a supermarket in Hong Kong

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.840
and the shelves are empty.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.760
At some stores they've started limiting

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:07.690
how much you can buy,

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:10.843
staples like canned food or toilet paper.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:13.880
- [Narrator] Panic buying is just one way

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.610
people in Hong Kong have reacted

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:18.100
as the government has put
in draconian restrictions

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.270
to control the fast
spreading Omicron variant.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:22.510
For about two years,

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:24.870
the city largely shut out COVID 19

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.210
but it has been fighting
a record surge in cases

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.823
that's overwhelmed hospitals.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:31.600
A low vaccination rate among the elderly

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:32.960
has also driven its death rate

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.360
to the highest in the world.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:39.550
So here's how everyday life
in Hong Kong has changed

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:42.193
and why many are rushing
to leave Asia's global hub?

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.840
Here in the city, daily
life has become complicated,

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.473
forcing many to reevaluate
Hong Kong as home.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:52.080
Vaccine passports are now required

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.330
to get around the city

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:56.433
and the unvaccinated can't
shop in supermarkets and malls.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.080
Summer break for students
started earlier in March

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.610
instead of July because the
government closed schools

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:03.700
so they could be converted

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:05.893
into testing and isolation centers.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.040
Gyms are shut too,

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.340
and people can't eat out after 6:00 PM,

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:12.090
which has hurt a lot of businesses.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:16.130
- This is Hong Kong
central business district.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:18.870
Around lunchtime
restaurants used to be busy

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:21.190
with bankers and lawyers,

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:22.730
but these days it's pretty quiet

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:26.180
and a lot of restaurants
and stores have had to shut.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:27.930
- [Narrator] Government
resources have also been pulled

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:29.650
to battle the outbreak.

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:31.980
Authorities have been quickly
building temporary hospitals

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.793
and massive isolation sites.

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:36.740
There's also a dedicated taxi fleet

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:38.373
to ferry the sick to clinics.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.810
But some government proposals
which have been integral

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:44.520
to China's ability to
quickly tame COVID spikes

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.683
have sparked panic among residents.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.740
In late February, local health authority

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.240
said the government couldn't rule out

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.050
whether to impose a citywide lockdown

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:54.903
to test an entire population.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:56.890
Fearing the worst,

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:58.990
residents scramble to
stock upon everything

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:01.040
from toiletries to food,

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:03.660
leaving many store shelves empty.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.800
A few days later this
city's chief executive

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:09.080
said there were no plans
for a wholesale lockdown.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:10.850
Instead she said the government's priority

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:13.850
would be reducing the number
of deaths and severe illnesses.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.740
But the government's
messaging hasn't been enough

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:19.663
to convince many residents to stay.

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:22.190
- This is Central Station.

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:25.320
It used to be one of Hong
Kong's busiest metro stops.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.450
A few months ago, it was bustling.

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:29.790
And this emptiness now is just one sign

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:32.393
of the sheer number of
people this city is losing.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:34.920
- [Narrator] According
to immigration data,

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:38.390
nearly 69,000 more Hong Kong
residents have left the city

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:39.860
and arrived this year,

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:42.280
with almost 80% of those
leaving in February

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:44.980
as the city's pandemic
controls kicked into full gear.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:49.060
Hong Kong officials have called for calm

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:50.140
and reassured residents

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:53.230
there would be enough supplies
of food and essentials.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:55.470
But as pressure from
business groups has mounted,

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:57.320
authorities in late March said the city

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:59.610
would scrap flight ban from some countries

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.570
and cut quarantine for returning residents

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:03.750
from 14 days to seven.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.550
The government also said it would relax

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:08.250
some social distancing rules from April.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.610
But China is also facing
its biggest outbreak

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:12.230
since the start of the pandemic

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:14.090
and authorities they
have kicked into action

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:16.940
by ordering millions to stay
home and restricting travel.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:20.250
However, Chinese president
Xi Jinping has vowed

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:22.890
to reduce the impacts of
those measures on the economy

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.203
and on people's lives.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.300
Health authorities have
also said that patients

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.190
with no symptoms or mild ones

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:31.070
should go to isolation facilities,

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:32.823
freeing up space in hospitals.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.310
It's a small step in easing restrictions,

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:37.990
but as long as Hong Kong remains aligned

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:39.320
with China's policies,

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:41.310
life in the city won't return to normal

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:43.510
until the number of
cases are under control.

